From: Lukas Rusak <lorusak@gmail.com>
Subject: avcodec/v4l2m2m: output DRM PRIME frames (dmabuf), implement hwcontext and flush

Firefox's V4L2 M2M path (FFmpegVideoDecoder::CreateImageV4L2) takes
mFrame->data[0] as an AVDRMFrameDescriptor and imports the dmabuf; upstream
FFmpeg's v4l2m2m decoders return NV12 copies in system memory, so Firefox
read the Y plane as a descriptor and dropped the hardware decoder after the
first frame.  This series (written for Kodi, carried by LibreELEC and by the
Raspberry Pi FFmpeg) lets the decoder output AV_PIX_FMT_DRM_PRIME frames
that point at the V4L2 capture buffers (exported with VIDIOC_EXPBUF), with
NV12 still offered for callers that ask for software frames:

  1/8 v4l2m2m: output AVDRMFrameDescriptor
  2/8 v4l2m2m: depends on libdrm
  3/8 v4l2m2m: set format_modifier to DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR
  4/8 v4l2m2m: only mmap the buffer when it is output type and drm prime is used
  5/8 v4l2m2m: allow using software pixel formats
  6/8 v4l2m2m: implement hwcontext
  7/8 v4l2m2m: add option to specify pixel format
  8/8 v4l2m2m: implement flush

Origin: LibreELEC.tv 4fada3363c (FFmpeg 6.0.1),
 packages/multimedia/ffmpeg/patches/v4l2-drmprime/ffmpeg-001-v4l2-drmprime.patch
 (Lukas Rusak, 2018-2020), squashed.  Adapted to Ubuntu's 6.1.1: the decoder
 definition macro has no FF_CODEC_CAP_SETS_PKT_DTS in 6.1, so the
 pix_fmts/hw_configs lines (patches 6/8 and 7/8) were placed by hand.
Forwarded: not-needed (out-of-tree series)
Last-Update: 2026-10-27
